        <mxCell id="HE9_o1VtQzB8J46Ih7h8-154" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Notes :&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;A public subnet is defined by its route to the IGW.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;A NAT gateway must be in a public subnet for public IPV4 egress.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Same-AZ private-to-NAT routing avoids an unnecessary cross-AZ dependency.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;SG is stateful; NACL is stateless.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Peering is non-transitive; Transit gateway is transitive hub.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Gateway endpoint is the preferred private S3/DynamoDB path.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
